<script lang="ts">
	import type { UIContainerSize } from '@meekojs/ui'

	import { examples } from '../../utils/examples'

	const sizes = ['sm', 'md', 'lg', 'xl', '2xl', '3xl', '4k', 'full'] as const
	const size = signal<UIContainerSize>('xl')
</script>

<template>
	<DocsPage
		locale="en"
		title="Container"
		description="Center your content and adapt its width from mobile to 4K screens."
	>
		<h2 id="usage">A width for each kind of content</h2>
		<p>Container takes the available width of its parent up to the chosen limit. It does not scale the typography or stretch the columns: it controls the space of the composition.</p>
		<div class="container-controls">
			<label for="container-size">Maximum width</label>
			<select
				id="container-size"
				bind:value="size.value"
				on:change="
					(event) => {
						const selected = sizes.find((value) => value === event.currentTarget.value)
						if (selected) size.value = selected
					}
				"
			>
				<option
					each:of="sizes"
					each:as="item"
					each:key="item"
					bind:value="item"
				>
					{item}
				</option>
			</select>
		</div>
		<div class="container-preview">
			<UIContainer
				as="section"
				ariaLabel="Container preview"
				class="container-example"
				bind:size="size.value"
			>
				<div class="container-content">
					<strong>A space for your interface</strong>
					<p>The container uses size={size.value} and gutter=md.</p>
				</div>
			</UIContainer>
		</div>
		<p>
			The preview is limited by this documentation column. In your application,
			<code>4k</code>
			allows an outer width of up to
			<code>240rem</code>
			: 3840 CSS pixels with a 16px root font.
		</p>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.container" />
		<h2 id="sizes">Maximum widths</h2>
		<DocsApi
			caption="Container sizes"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'sm', type: '40rem', description: '640px. Forms and compact content.' },
				{ name: 'md', type: '48rem', description: '768px. Reading and settings.' },
				{ name: 'lg', type: '64rem', description: '1024px. Application content.' },
				{ name: 'xl', type: '80rem', description: '1280px. Default value.' },
				{ name: '2xl', type: '96rem', description: '1536px. Wide panels.' },
				{ name: '3xl', type: '120rem', description: '1920px. Large desktop views.' },
				{ name: '4k', type: '240rem', description: '3840px. Work surfaces in 4K.' },
				{ name: 'full', type: 'none', description: 'No limit: takes the available width of the parent.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>The pixel equivalents use a 16px root. The behavior depends on the CSS viewport, not on the physical resolution of the monitor. On screens wider than the maximum, the content stays centered.</p>
		<h2 id="gutters">Adaptive side spacing</h2>
		<p>
			<code>gutter</code>
			adds logical padding on both sides, included in the outer width. The
			<code>md</code>
			value grows between 16 and 64px;
			<code>sm</code>
			, between 12 and 24px;
			<code>lg</code>
			, between 24 and 96px. Use
			<code>none</code>
			when the parent already provides that space.
		</p>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.containerNested" />
		<div class="doc-note">A 4K container does not make all the text 3840px wide. Combine a wide surface with smaller containers for reading, forms and details.</div>
		<h2 id="api">API</h2>
		<DocsApi
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'size', type: 'UIContainerSize', default: 'xl', description: 'Maximum width. sm, md, lg, xl, 2xl, 3xl, 4k or full.' },
				{ name: 'gutter', type: 'none | sm | md | lg', default: 'md', description: 'Fluid side padding with RTL direction support.' },
				{ name: 'as', type: 'UIContainerTag', default: 'div', description: 'div, section, main, article, header, footer, nav or aside.' },
				{ name: 'id / ariaLabel / class', type: 'string', description: 'Identity, accessible name and additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			It requires the
			<code>default</code>
			snippet. It adds no roles, headings or interactive behavior. Choose
			<code>as</code>
			according to the semantics of the content; do not nest another
			<code>main</code>
			inside the main one.
		</p>
		<h2 id="customize">Customization</h2>
		<p>
			Use a class to override
			<code>--meeko-ui-container-max-width</code>
			or
			<code>--meeko-ui-container-gutter</code>
			. The container does not hide overflowing content: tables and code blocks must manage their own scroll.
		</p>
		<DocsCode
			label="app/styles/main.css"
			bind:code="examples.containerCss"
		/>
	</DocsPage>
</template>

<style>
	.container-controls {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin: 1.5rem 0;
		font-size: 0.875rem;
	}
	.container-controls select {
		border: 1px solid var(--ui-color-border-strong);
		border-radius: var(--ui-radius-md);
		background: var(--ui-color-surface);
		padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
		color: var(--ui-color-text);
		font: inherit;
	}
	.container-preview {
		border-block: 1px solid var(--ui-color-border);
		padding-block: 2rem;
	}
	.container-example {
		border-inline: 1px dashed var(--ui-color-primary);
		background: var(--ui-color-primary-soft);
	}
	.container-content {
		padding-block: 2rem;
	}
	.container-content p {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}
</style>
